oncatenate the attended outputs, and pass through a classifier head (384→128→3). This follows successful historical exp 1 that used cross-attention fusion to improve feature interaction over simple gating, addressing the initial plan's root cause of indiscriminate feature mixing.", "training_evaluation": "Replace the current linear scheduler with AdamW optimizer (weight_decay=1e-3) and a cosine annealing learning rate schedule with linear warmup for 5 epochs. This directly addresses the plateau observed (val log-loss 0.515) by providing aggressive early exploration and smoother convergence, as successful historical experiments showed. Implementation: use torch.optim.lr_scheduler.CosineAnnealingLR after a warmup phase (warmup_steps=5*len(train_loader)), and keep other training settings (batch size 1024, early stopping patience 7, gradient clipping) unchanged."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
